    "result_text": "The build is green. The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain blocklist rule for owner creation. When the owner's email domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), the create is rejected with **400 Bad Request**.\n\nChanges, following the codebase's existing field-validation conventions:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `rest/advice/DisposableEmailException.java`, a subclass of the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldException`. This means it's automatically handled by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` as a 400 (no new handler needed), consistent with how `InvalidTelephoneException` and `InvalidPostcodeException` work.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` blocklist constant and a `rejectDisposableEmailDomain(...)` guard, invoked from `normalizeOwnerFields` right after the email is canonicalized (lower-cased). The domain (part after the final `@`) is compared case-insensitively against the blocklist; a `null` email (email is optional) or one without a domain part is left untouched.\n\nThe check runs on the create path after email normalization, matching where the existing postcode/telephone field validations live. Full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` acceptance test.",
